---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Publishing roadmap — Auspicious Music"
  description="Guides and resources shown in the design that are still being tested, researched, or cleared for publication."
  canonicalPath="/publishing-roadmap/"
  noindex={true}
>
  <main id="content">
    <section class="pg-head">
      <div class="shell">
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li>Publishing roadmap</li></ol></nav>
        <h1>What is still being built</h1>
        <p class="lede">Some items in this pre-launch design are editorial commitments, not finished articles. They stay out of the index until the workflow, examples, versions, and rights checks are complete.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band band--tight">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2 style="margin-top:0">Planned practical guides</h2>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>DAW project guidelines for reliable music production</li>
            <li>Live strings versus sample libraries</li>
            <li>Production music licensing: a practical introduction</li>
            <li>What Max for Live is and where it changes a workflow</li>
            <li>A repeatable Ableton project template</li>
            <li>Recording and arranging music for film, video, and ceremonies</li>
          </ul>
          <h2>Publication gate</h2>
          <p>A technical article is published only after its software version, test date, examples, limitations, and sources are recorded. A legacy resource is published only after ownership and redistribution rights are clear.</p>
          <p><a class="link" href="/about/editorial-policy/">Read the editorial policy
            <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg>
          </a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
